 and that  they are reassuring people that if they  come forward these uh the any  information can be treated anonymously  there are numerous ways numerous ways  that people can get in touch with them  either directly they can do it through  crime stoppers which is anonymous they  can upload any footage that they've got  from cctv cameras mobile phones anything  like that on a secure portal that's  available through the merseyside police  website so we know that the local  council here set up drop-in centers for  people to come in if they don't want to  deal with the police directly they can  go and talk to local councillors in  confidence that their that their  identities won't necessarily be revealed  and that those councillors will then  pass that information out to police uh  if they keep saying all the way through  these investigations it's the public  that will hold the key to this someone  will know the name of the person  responsible for this and uh and of  course there are the there's the wall of  science that you're talking about the  grass culture that people keep referring  to here you know people will be scared  these are dangerous people and there  will of course be concerns amongst  people for their own safety for the  safeties  for the safety of their families whether  or not they are identified as someone  who's giving information to police but  people are coming forward and they are  helping and progress does seem to be  being made  okay fraser thank you very much indeed  that's the update then on the murder of  olivia pratt corbell we were also given  updates on sam rimmer three arrests have  been made on suspicion of murder  he was killed in liverpool on the 16th  of august also ashley dale killed on the  21st of august a man arrested on  suspicion of murder a woman arrested on  assisting an offender so clearly this  investigation is continuing at a pace as  we heard from merseyside police they are  pleased with the information that they  are getting from members of the public  but of course they are appealing for  more information for cctv for names  anything at all that could lead them to  the man responsible for this horrific  attack on a little girl on monday nights

